      "text": "BREAKING NEWS Philippines :  (  Again ) The magnitude 6.2 earthquake near Cagwait, Surigao del Sur, on October 11 at 10:32 p.m. highlights the seismic activity in the region, which is part of the Pacific Ring of Fire, known for its frequent and sometimes destructive earthquakes. The Philippine Institute of Volcanology and Seismology (PHIVOLCS) monitors such events closely, providing updates and safety advisories to help communities respond effectively. It is crucial for residents in the area to stay alert for potential aftershocks, follow safety protocols, and prepare emergency kits and plans to mitigate damage and ensure safety.\n\nSource : Inquirer",
